 "notes": [
  "the real-capital ratio is published through 2019 and extended to 2024 in ratio space. The extended values are computed, not published, and any output using them carries the extension label.",
  "the stimulus proxy is net new credit, not the fiscal balance, because for this economy the discretionary injection runs mostly through credit rather than through the budget. It is derived from BIS total credit and World Bank output by a stated method, so it is a computed input rather than a published one, and it is not comparable against an economy measured on the fiscal balance.",
  "the credit saturation axis carries an uplift of 1.40, because BIS total credit to the non-financial sector omits credit to the financial sector and much non-bank intermediation. The uplift flows into K_I, since K_I is the saturation ratio times output. It is a level adjustment, so growth rates, direction and turning points are unchanged, and it is applied identically to every economy, so the cross-section ordering is unchanged.",
  "K_I is BIS total credit to the non-financial sector only. Listed equity market capitalisation is excluded because it is not comparable across economies and its vintages differ by up to seven years, so including it would make a cross-section incoherent.",
  "the highest published capital-to-output ratio over the window is 5.00, which makes the investment share r = 1 - K_R/Y equal -4.00 at that point. Wherever r is negative the reduced output equation Y_dot = (p_b Y + r K_I + S) / 2 drives output towards zero, so the system does not integrate. A common scale of 0.1801 applied to both capital stocks brings the maximum K_R/Y to 0.90, so r stays positive for every period and section 0.2's definition of it as a share holds throughout. The scale is applied to both stocks, so K_R/K_I and therefore the Phase 4 condition are unchanged, and being multiplicative it cannot alter growth rates, direction or turning points. The consequence is that K_R/Y cannot cross one inside the calibration window, so the production-versus-financial transition of section 0.5 is not observable on the normalised path.",
  "K_R is reconstructed as the Penn World Table capital-to-output ratio multiplied by market-valued output, so it is market-valued by construction and no PPP conversion factor is involved. It is a reconstruction rather than a published level."
 ]
}